{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 11, :comments ["<b>Pass over a transgression</b> — that one pass over it so as to distance himself from it, and this is the way of a proverb. For one who wishes to take vengeance stands over the transgression, and 'bearing iniquity' is as though one passed over it and left it." "<b>Is slow</b> — a past-tense verb going out to the actual [present] action, and its meaning, [understood] by the intellect, is: one lengthens a man's nose." "<b>And his glory</b> — that others glorify him, upon his passing over a transgression."], :book :proverbs, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 19, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Proverbs -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/mishley/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:23:37.897859406Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}